@@ -65,6 +65,23 @@ for this source.
 - `vz2wav-decompile-main/` (your repo) — source for `vzpack`/`vz2wav`/`wav2vz`. `dist/linux.zip` has working prebuilt x86-64 binaries despite the `ia64-linux` directory name.
 - `z88dk-master.zip` — source for `z88dk-z80asm`. Needs 4 git submodules (`uthash`, `optparse`, `regex`, `UNIXem`) that a plain GitHub zip download doesn't include.
 
+## Font table (corrected, embedded)
+
+The VZ200 ROM's `PRN_GFX_FONT` (0x3B94) has 17 bad bytes across 10 glyphs
+(`VZ200_basic_ROM_listing/README-Font issue.md`; confirmed against a real
+ROM dump). The ROM can't be patched, so `port_13ghosts_v7.py` now parses
+`VZ200_basic_ROM_listing/corrected_table.asm`, emits it into the game image
+as `vz_font_src` (320 bytes, after the HAL), and `vz_build_font_cache`
+reads that copy -- the ROM font is no longer touched. `make` rebuilds
+automatically when `corrected_table.asm` changes. Stage 1 is unchanged.
+
+`verify_hud_render.py NEW.bin NEW.map OLD.bin OLD.map` runs the real boot + `vz_draw_hud_row` for a new and an old (ROM-font) build and renders the HUD strip to `hud_render_corrected_font.png` (maps from `z88dk-z80asm -b -m`).
+
+`verify_font_cache.py` runs the real boot path in the Z80 emulator with the
+ROM font region deliberately poisoned and checks the 1024-byte tile cache
+against an independent Python reference; it also writes
+`font_cache_corrected.png`. (`pip install z80 pillow`.)
+
 ---
 
